WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.669
-Hey, everyone.
It is the end of the week.

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.037
That's usually when I catch up
on some personal stuff.

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:06.339
I check my inbox, return emails,
and of course,

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:07.640
I send out thank you notes.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.709
And I was just wondering if I
could write out a couple

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.911
thank you notes right now,
if that's okay with you guys.

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.646
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:17.183
James, could I get some thank
you note writing music, please?

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:19.952
[ Piano playing ]
Thank you very much.

00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:22.455
[ Note trills ]

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:23.889
Oh, stop.
You know you gave a little

00:00:23.889 --> 00:00:25.458
r-r-ring on that little --

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:27.126
♪ Da-da-rrring ♪

00:00:27.126 --> 00:00:29.962
[ Note trills ]

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:31.230 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:34.000 line:0%
Thank you,
Sony's new PlayStation 5,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.502 line:0%
or as I call you,
the reverse Oreo.

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:39.038 line:0%
[ Piano music stops ]
[ Scattered laughter ]

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:40.740 line:0%
[ Soft slurp ]

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.842 line:0%
I love when you can hear me lick
the envelope.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:45.477 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.477 --> 00:00:49.515 line:0%
Makes you feel good.
Wakes you up a little bit.

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:50.817 line:0%
[ Clears throat ]

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:52.018 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:53.953 line:0%
Thank you, new Apple Watch,

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:56.689 line:0%
for being able to measure
blood oxygen levels.

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:59.592 line:0%
That's great info to have
right after I get a notification

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:01.594 line:0%
that Grubhub is here
with my cheesesteak.

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:04.931 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:09.101 line:0%
[ Mimics slurp ]
-I wish.

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:10.536 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:14.039 line:0%
Thank you, Joe Biden's CNN
town hall drive-in

00:01:14.039 --> 00:01:17.610 line:0%
for inspiring a lot of people
with your message of unity

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.079 line:0%
and really confusing one family
who thought they were there

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:25.819 line:0%
to see "Scoob."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:27.787 line:0%
-Spot on.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:31.391 line:0%
-Thank you.

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:33.393 line:0%
-Spot on.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:35.728 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:37.096 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:37.096 --> 00:01:39.932 line:0%
-Thank you,
President Obama's new memoir,

00:01:39.932 --> 00:01:42.868 line:0%
for being 768 pages long.

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:47.307 line:0%
Although, to be fair, 600 of
those pages are just "Uhh."

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:49.909 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:57.617 line:0%
That was for you.
That was for you, Barack.

00:01:57.617 --> 00:02:00.520 line:0%
[ As Barack Obama ] Uhhhhhhhh...

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.388 line:0%
Jimmy!

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:05.424 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:06.825 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:06.825 --> 00:02:08.761 line:0%
-Thank you, Easy Mac,

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.497 line:0%
for being there for those of us

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:13.199 line:0%
who can't quite handle
difficult mac.

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:17.703 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.703 --> 00:02:20.073 line:0%
[ Southern accent ] 82
ingredients?

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:24.010 line:0%
The heck kind of macaroni
and cheese is this?

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:28.180 line:0%
Well, first I guess I got
to grate the cheese,

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:32.285 line:0%
put it in the dehumidifier,
and dry it.

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:37.957 line:0%
Then I put it in the Cuisinart
and pulverize it

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:43.730 line:0%
into said powder,
and then I have to --

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:46.799 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:48.367 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:51.103 line:0%
[ Normal voice ] Thank you,
smirks, for letting me know

00:02:51.103 --> 00:02:53.873 line:0%
which members of a Zoom meeting
are DM-ing each other.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:56.809 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:02.548 line:0%
That's a thinker, man.
-Yeah.

00:03:02.548 --> 00:03:05.084 line:0%
-I started with a stinker,
ended with a thinker.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:07.086 line:0%
-Yep.

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:09.121 line:0%
Hmm.

00:03:09.121 --> 00:03:10.490 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.692 line:0%
-Thank you,
shopping for a mattress,

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.693 line:0%
for being a great way to show
strangers

00:03:14.693 --> 00:03:17.363 line:0%
the weird positions
you sleep in.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.666 line:0%
Let me try this thing out.

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:21.701 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:27.673 line:0%
Are you a fetal position dude?

00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:32.612 line:0%
-I'm like, you know, I guess
a grass hopper position.

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:33.913 line:0%
-Like a praying mantis
type of deal?

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:38.584 line:0%
-Kind of. I use my arm as, like,
a pillow, the one arm,

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:41.187 line:0%
but then I take this arm
and I sort of go like this.

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:43.322 line:0%
-Where's the pillow?

00:03:43.322 --> 00:03:45.624 line:0%
-My arm is the pillow.
-No pillow?

00:03:45.624 --> 00:03:48.461 line:0%
-Sometimes the pillow would
be underneath this arm.

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:50.329 line:0%
-Yeah, stack it around?
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:52.832 line:0%
I get my stack on.
-I started doing full on

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:55.134 line:0%
just like that.
-That's just --

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:57.203 line:0%
Like, come on, man.
-Like water slide.

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:59.539 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
I water slide to sleep.

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:01.306 line:0%
That's it.
And then during the night,

00:04:01.306 --> 00:04:02.975 line:0%
I'll wake up or something like
that, and then sometimes,

00:04:02.975 --> 00:04:06.045 line:0%
I'll do the plunge...
-Oh, man.

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:08.281 line:0%
-...full face down.
And then I try that.

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:09.815 line:0%
Doesn't quite work.
Nancy doesn't like it.

00:04:09.815 --> 00:04:12.618 line:0%
So one arm will go in.

00:04:12.618 --> 00:04:15.788 line:0%
You know?
My back's all screwed up.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:20.192 line:0%
-Michelle sleeps with one leg
up, but it never stays up.

00:04:20.192 --> 00:04:22.528 line:0%
If I wake up and her leg is up,

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:27.500 line:0%
then I'm kept awake by the sound
of it gradually slipping down.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:30.803 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:33.639 line:0%
Her foot just like sliding down
the sheet.

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:34.941 line:0%
-Come on. Get it over with.

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:37.310 line:0%
-It's like, "uhhhhhhhh."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:39.211 line:0%
-Creeping along, yeah?
-Sometimes I like

00:04:39.211 --> 00:04:41.814 line:0%
just knock her leg down and just
act like I'm asleep again.

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:47.186 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:49.588 line:0%
-Ah, here we go.
The last thank you note.

00:04:49.588 --> 00:04:50.923 line:0%
-Aww.
-Aww.

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:53.091 line:0%
-Aww.
-But it was...

00:04:53.091 --> 00:04:55.228 line:0%
[ Somber music plays ]

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:57.863 line:0%
[ Voice breaking ]
It was so fun.

00:04:57.863 --> 00:05:01.533 line:0%
We had some bad ones.

00:05:01.533 --> 00:05:03.269 line:0%
We had some good ones.

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:04.971 line:0%
-Did we, though?

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:06.439 line:0%
-Yeah. We definitely had
some good ones.

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:07.573 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:10.677 line:0%
That first one was not bad,
was it?

00:05:10.677 --> 00:05:14.346 line:0%
No, the PlayStation 5,
reverse Oreo.

00:05:14.346 --> 00:05:15.915 line:0%
-Yeah.
-That was pretty good.

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:17.817 line:0%
It's a joke for the future.

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:19.451 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.451 --> 00:05:20.886 line:0%
-It's your birthday, man,
go ahead.

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:22.855 line:0%
-Yeah, thanks, man.
-You're welcome.

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:26.025 line:0%
[ Clears throat ]

00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:27.993 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:27.993 --> 00:05:29.962 line:0%
-Thank you, Batman,

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:32.164 line:0%
for being an anti-masker
despite the fact

00:05:32.164 --> 00:05:34.100 line:0%
that you're wearing a mask.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.736 line:0%
There you have it.
Those are my thank you notes.

